From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: videobuf2: default the core helpers on

VIDEOBUF2_CORE, VIDEOBUF2_V4L2 and VIDEOBUF2_MEMOPS are hidden
tristates selected by in-tree drivers. Out-of-tree camera drivers
(the T20 tx-isp module) need them exported, but there is no visible
symbol to turn them on. Default them on whenever the media stack is
enabled.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
--- a/drivers/media/common/videobuf2/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/media/common/videobuf2/Kconfig
@@ -3,12 +3,15 @@
 config VIDEOBUF2_CORE
 	select DMA_SHARED_BUFFER
 	tristate
+	default y if MEDIA_SUPPORT
 
 config VIDEOBUF2_V4L2
 	tristate
+	default y if MEDIA_SUPPORT
 
 config VIDEOBUF2_MEMOPS
 	tristate
+	default y if MEDIA_SUPPORT
 
 config VIDEOBUF2_DMA_CONTIG
 	tristate
